'''Dragonite Island''' (Japanese: '''カイリューの{{tt|島|しま}}''' ''{{tt|Kairyu|Dragonite}} Island'') is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive location located off the coast of the [[Kanto]] [[region]]. It was featured in ''[[JN010|A Test in Paradise!]]''.

Dragonite Island is an island solely populated by members of the {{p|Dratini}} [[evolution]]ary line. It has a beach, forests, a river, and a waterfall. Behind the waterfall is a small cave where local Dratini like to shed their skin. The local {{p|Dragonair}} use their weather-controlling powers to create constant storms around the island to keep it hidden, though the {{p|Dragonite}} living on the island sometimes take shipwrecked people there to recover. It is also located in an area without {{wp|Global Positioning System|GPS}} coverage, making the task of pinpointing its location impossible.

{{Ash}} and [[Goh]] visited the island after hearing rumors of its existence from [[Professor Cerise]]. During their visit, Ash helped a Dragonair learn how to fly. Shortly afterwards, it evolved into a {{AP|Dragonite}} and chose to join Ash's [[party|team]]. Ash and Goh later told Professor Cerise about the island, but he chose to keep its existence a secret from the public to keep the mystery surrounding it alive.

